    "rows": "\"=o/n\" equal (old line o, new line n), \"-o\" delete, \"+n\" insert, suffix \"mK\" = moveId K. Display order: matched lines in order; between two matched lines all deletes, then all inserts.",
    "moves": "\"id:oldLine>newLine\"",
    "stats": "unchanged + removed + moved = old line count; unchanged + added + moved = new line count (a move is counted once)",
    "validatedDocuments": "complete documents for the runtime validator of results from Rust and the Web Worker (src/utils/diff/validate.ts): valid ones and deliberately corrupted ones with matching counts and statistics. JS only: Rust produces documents but never receives them; its test invariants check the same rules."
